  (text "TPS3700 reference: positive396..404mV; negative387..400mV.\nInclude0.1percent divider errors and +/-25nA input bias.\nStatic SYS UV fall min3.4246V; OV rise max4.8596V.\nWith ASSUMED switch+harness drop<=50mV: LCD>=3.3746V.\nMain3.3V fixed PWM:3.267..3.333V; no ripple/transient guarantee.\nTCA sideA=main3.3V; sideB=switched SYS. Off I2C must stay high-Z.\nEN high follows switched VCCB through U23, R53/R54.\nLCD total C<=100uF and aggregate off injection<=20uA MUST be measured.\nHardware hold180ms minus ASSUMED turn-off<=5ms permits discharge.\nServices stay locked during startup, undervoltage and all faults.\nFast pulses, backfeed, input budget, temperature and RF remain unqualified."
    (at 195 112 0)
